From: Tilo <noreply@tilo.so>
Subject: [PATCH] install: --source-booted copies the booted image as it is stored

`bootc install to-filesystem --source-booted` installs the image this system
booted by copying it out of the booted composefs repository into the
target's, as `cfsctl oci copy` does: manifest, config and layers as they are
stored, each layer checked against its diff id on the way in. It runs on the
host, with no container engine. An installer used to export the booted image
as an OCI layout, load that into container storage and have bootc pull it
back out, writing the whole image three times to install it once and giving
the installed deployment the export's manifest digest instead of the booted
image's. The disk space check reads the manifest from the booted repository.
It prints how long the copy took, beside the install's other steps.
---
